  "id": "20_Leaders_Who_Built_the_CISO_Era_2_Decades_of_Change_txt_103",
  "content": "Metasploit's creator, renowned security expert HD Moore, first released the tool in 2003, at a time when security researchers were either ignored or reviled by technology vendors for sharing their findings of product vulnerabilities. There were no bug-bounty programs, no responsible disclosure processes, so Moore often grabbed vendors' attention by releasing his bug discoveries to the public, often much to the dismay of companies such as Microsoft . His controversial and enlightening Month of Browser Bugs (MoBB) project in the summer of 2006 dropped daily demo code of security flaws he discovered in popular browsers, including Internet Explorer and Mozilla. MoBB made Moore's point about poor browser security loud and clear, pressuring vendors to build more secure versions of their software.",
  "category": "Article",
  "source": "Local Storage",
